==English==

===Etymology===
{{rfe|lang=en}}

Southern man living on a farm used to shoot "cow piles" in his front yard. He got a phone call from his friend asking what he was doing. His response...

"Nothing just shooting the shit, you can come over if you like." Hence "Shooting the shit" was born.

===Verb===
{{head|en|verb}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic|vulgar}} To [[chat]] [[casually]]; to [[gossip]].
#: ''We didn't do much besides stand around and '''shoot the shit''', but it was fun to see him again.''

